  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    { "@type": "Question", "name": "Which PFAS limits apply to drinking water in Germany?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Since 12 January 2026, the sum of 20 PFAS (Sum of PFAS-20) is limited to 0.0001 mg/l, i.e. 0.1 µg/l or 100 ng/l. From 12 January 2028, an additional limit of 0.00002 mg/l, i.e. 20 ng/l, applies to the sum of PFOA, PFNA, PFHxS and PFOS (Sum of PFAS-4). Both values are set out in Annex 2 of the German Drinking Water Ordinance (TrinkwV)." } },
